<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">France-Albert René</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1935">1935</a>–<a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">France-Albert René was a Seychellois lawyer and socialist leader who became prime minister at independence in 1976. In June 1977, while President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-mancham">James Mancham</a> was abroad, his supporters seized power in a coup, and René became president. He ruled a one-party state until multiparty elections were restored in 1993, which he won, and stepped down in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france-albert-rene.jpg" alt="France-Albert René" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seychelles Nation · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:France_Albert-Ren%C3%A9.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
